  <p>{{ site.rights.notice }}</p>
  <p><strong>Usage terms:</strong> {{ site.rights.terms }}</p>
  <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
  <p>This is a demonstration of rights and description metadata for agencies. Each image on the site carries the same description in three machine-readable places:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>HTML <code>alt</code></strong> – read by screen readers, crawlers and multimodal models that parse the page.</li>
    <li><strong>XMP inside the file</strong> – <code>Iptc4xmpCore:AltTextAccessibility</code>, <code>dc:description</code>, <code>dc:rights</code>, <code>xmpRights:WebStatement</code>, <code>plus:LicensorURL</code>. It travels with the file when it's downloaded, scraped or ingested into a DAM or training set.</li>
    <li><strong>schema.org JSON-LD</strong> – <code>ImageObject</code> with <code>description</code>, <code>copyrightNotice</code>, <code>license</code> and <code>acquireLicensePage</code>, the fields Google Images uses for its Licensable badge.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>When the three agree, a model or index doesn't have to guess what an image shows or who controls it.</p>
  <h2>Images</h2>
